# Required Reality Summary

After the specification result or implementation meta-prompt, append:

REALITY SUMMARY

Write exactly two short plain-English paragraphs followed by zero to ten optional bullets.

The first paragraph must identify:

- The selected delivery mode;
- The artifact produced;
- Where it was written or returned;
- Whether the artifact itself has been executed.

The second paragraph must state:

- The concrete user-visible, system-visible, operational, or project result that would exist if the feature were implemented according to the artifact.

Use bullets only for distinct essential outputs, phases, behaviors, constraints, or effects that materially clarify the implemented reality.

Every bullet must be one complete sentence.

The reality summary must:

- Describe the artifact accurately;
- Distinguish specification creation from feature implementation;
- Use conditional or future language for unimplemented behavior;
- Use completed language only for work actually performed;
- Describe what the resulting feature would do in reality;
- Describe material user or system effects;
- Describe material workflow phases when useful;
- Avoid evaluating or grading the specification;
- Avoid gap analysis;
- Avoid recommendations;
- Avoid introducing new requirements;
- Avoid adding another implementation plan;
- Avoid directing the user to another prompt;
- Avoid claiming that the target feature already exists;
- Avoid claiming verification that did not occur.

The reality summary is a synopsis of the feature’s implemented reality, not a summary of the prompt-writing process.

